questions.question:
The standard reduction potential data at $25^{o}$C is given below:

$E^{o}$ ($Fe^{3+}$ , $Fe^{2+}$) = +0.77V;

$E^{o}$ ($Fe^{2+}$ , Fe) = -0.44V;

$E^{o}$ ($Cu^{2+}$ , Cu) = +0.34V;

$E^{o}$ ($Cu^{+}$ , Cu) = +0.52V;

$E^{o}$ [$O_{2}$(g) + $4H^{+} + 4e^{-} \to 2H_{2}$O] = +1.23V;

$E^{o}$ [$O_{2}$(g) + $2H_{2}$O + $4e^{-} \to 4OH^{-}$] = +0.40 V

$E^{o}$ ($Cr^{3+}$ , Cr) = -0.74V;

$E^{o}$ ($Cr^{2+}$ , Cr) = -0.91V;

Match $E^{o}$ of the redox pair in List – I with the values given in List – II and select the correct answer using the code given below the lists:



**List - I**

P. $E^{o}$ ($Fe^{3+}$ , Fe)

Q. $E^{o}$ ($4H_{2}$O $\leftrightharpoons 4H^{+} + 4OH^{-}$)

R. $E^{o}$ ($Cu^{2+}$  + Cu $\to 2Cu^{+}$)

S. $E^{o}$ ($Cr^{3+}$, $Cr^{2+}$)



**List - II**

1. -0.18 V

2. -0.4 V

3. -0.04 V

4. -0.83 V

